.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rqx 1  "rqx " 
.SH NAME
rqx \- Reports dead code, duplication, complexity and architectural drift in TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, Go, Java and C++, with the reason each finding matters
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrqx\fR [\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-motion\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR] [\fB\-\-progress\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-hyperlinks\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reports dead code, duplication, complexity and architectural drift in TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, Go, Java and C++, with the reason each finding matters
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR
Do not open the interactive interface; bare `rqx` prints the report instead
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour output; `auto` follows NO_COLOR and whether stdout is a terminal
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-motion\fR \fI<MOTION>\fR [default: on]
Animation in the interactive interface
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR
Do not draw the progress bar on stderr; `\-\-quiet` implies it
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI<PROGRESS>\fR [default: auto]
How a scan reports progress on stderr; `plain` prints a line every two seconds for a job log
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: A bar on a terminal, nothing in CI or when stderr is redirected
.IP \(bu 2
bar: A bar whenever stderr is a terminal, CI included
.IP \(bu 2
plain: A line on stderr every two seconds and at each phase, for a job log
.IP \(bu 2
none: Nothing
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase output: `\-v` adds the configuration, the cache and every skipped file to the report; `\-vv` also prints stage timings and git commands on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-hyperlinks\fR \fI<HYPERLINKS>\fR [default: auto]
Render `file:line` in the report as a hyperlink that opens in an editor; `auto` enables it on terminals known to support hyperlinks
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal known to support them
.IP \(bu 2
always: Whenever the report is coloured
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
rqx\-scan(1)
Analyze a project and report every finding
.TP
rqx\-fix(1)
Apply the fixes that have a single correct result, proving each one before it is written. Previews by default
.TP
rqx\-verify(1)
Compare the working tree against a base revision and classify each finding as resolved, improved, relocated or introduced
.TP
rqx\-setup(1)
Print the configuration an editor needs to connect to rqx, or list the supported editors
.TP
rqx\-plan(1)
Rank the work by value against effort, and report the health score after it
.TP
rqx\-explain(1)
Print the catalogue entry for a rule or a pattern: what it maps to, what decides it and what fixes it
.TP
rqx\-rules(1)
List every rule rqx can report, grouped by family
.TP
rqx\-baseline(1)
Record the findings this project already has, so the gate evaluates only what a change adds
.TP
rqx\-suppressions(1)
List every finding waived by a comment in the source, with its reason
.TP
rqx\-waive(1)
Waive one finding with a comment in the source that states a reason
.TP
rqx\-complexity(1)
Report the complexity distribution, with the highest values
.TP
rqx\-perf(1)
Report code whose work grows faster than its input, ranked by reach
.TP
rqx\-update(1)
Install the newest release, or report what it would change
.TP
rqx\-completions(1)
Print a shell completion script
.TP
rqx\-recommend(1)
Recommend actions for the project: configuration thresholds, refactorings, files to read and performance work
.TP
rqx\-slop(1)
Score files that show signs of not having been reviewed after they were written
.TP
rqx\-hotspots(1)
Rank files by how often they change and how much is wrong with them
.TP
rqx\-badge(1)
Write the health score as a small SVG badge
.TP
rqx\-health(1)
Break the health score down by component and report what removing each would gain
.TP
rqx\-graph(1)
Print the import graph as text, Graphviz, Mermaid or JSON
.TP
rqx\-cache(1)
Show what the analysis cache holds, or delete it
.TP
rqx\-query(1)
Run a tree\-sitter query over a project, to test it before adding it to a `rule` entry in `rqx.yaml`
.TP
rqx\-techniques(1)
List every refactoring rqx prescribes and the rules that prescribe it
.TP
rqx\-levels(1)
Print what each cleanliness level sets, as the equivalent configuration settings
.TP
rqx\-patterns(1)
Report which design patterns a project uses, which are half applied, and where one would fit
.TP
rqx\-check(1)
Analyze changed files against a base revision and fail if the gate is not met
.TP
rqx\-comment(1)
Post the review as a comment on its merge request, and grade the commit
.TP
rqx\-init(1)
Write a commented rqx.yaml with every setting at its default
.TP
rqx\-config(1)
Print the settings a run will use, and the file each one came from
.TP
rqx\-mcp(1)
Run as an MCP server, so an AI agent can query a project\*(Aqs findings
.TP
rqx\-lsp(1)
Run as a Language Server over stdio, for editor integration
